<article class="env-corollary" id="BD75">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/BD75">Corollary <span data-tag="BD75">7.2.4.16</span>.</a> Let $X$ be a Heyting space of finite Heyting dimension, and let $\calF $ be a strongly $k$-connective sheaf on $X$. Then $\calF (X)$ is $k$-connective. </p>
</article>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Apply Corollary <a href="/tag/AF10" data-tag="AF10">7.2.4.15</a> in the case where $Y$ is a point. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>